# Every format the scripts read, carrying an HTML comment: the template's
# example entries left in the compilation, a real entry with a note after it, a
# task and an architecture row with the same, and a commented-out `> Status:`
# line above the real one. What is inside a comment counts nowhere; what is
# outside one counts everywhere, and the same lines have to be real to a reader
# and to a writer.
#
# The blank `> Status:` and `> Verdict:` lines above the real ones are the same
# claim from the other side: a field line with no value is not the field, and a
# writer that landed on it would rewrite the line nothing reads and leave the
# old value standing where everything does.
FEATURE=Cart
GIT=yes
